From b718c5cf04bed39a06a335111c87f0880f3410d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:11:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Use SerialParam for nproc = 1 as intended

setUpBPPARAM() assigned SerialParam() for nproc == 1 and then
unconditionally overwrote it with MulticoreParam(workers = 1) (or
SnowParam on Windows), so nproc = 1 still forked a worker. Make the
platform branch an else-if. Results do not change: fgsea's random
streams are seeded before bplapply(), and the output with nproc = 1
is identical before and after this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TaHntBDKuZJpMAAMenkC44
---
 R/fgsea.R | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/R/fgsea.R b/R/fgsea.R
index efc2999..f8547f0 100644
--- a/R/fgsea.R
+++ b/R/fgsea.R
@@ -721,8 +721,7 @@ setUpBPPARAM <- function(nproc=0, BPPARAM=NULL){
         if (nproc != 0) {
             if (nproc == 1) {
                 result <- SerialParam(progressbar = TRUE)
-            }
-            if (.Platform$OS.type == "windows") {
+            } else if (.Platform$OS.type == "windows") {
                 # windows doesn't support multicore, using snow instead
                 result <- SnowParam(workers = nproc, progressbar = TRUE)
             } else {
